Representation - The electorate vote for [[MP]] who then speak up for the views of their constituents in parliament

Choosing government - The electorate vote for [[MP]], and then the party with the most [[MP]] is invited to form a government

Participation - Every registered voter gets to have a say

Influence over policy - The electorate vote for [[MP]] partly based on policies in a [[Manifesto]], giving MPs a [[mandate]] to pursue those policies

Accountability - The electorate can choose NOT to vote for a candidate if they disagree with the actions of that candidate or their party

Citizen education - Learn about current issues through the news, Reading [[Manifesto]]s<br>Learn about other people’s views, and (hopefully) how to be tolerant

Legitimacy Gives the governing party the right to pursue certain courses of action ([[mandate]])

Elite Recruitment - Elections help to select future leaders ministers
